    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add state partitioning notes to Web Storage API documentation]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45209</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45209"/>
        <updated>2026-08-18T03:13:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258725120?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h2 dir="auto">Description</h2>
<p dir="auto">This updates the Web Storage API documentation to mention <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Privacy/Guides/State_Partitioning" rel="nofollow">state partitioning</a>, which modern browsers use to partition storage by top-level site when accessed from third-party contexts.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Files changed</h3>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong>localStorage</strong> (): Added a paragraph in the Description section explaining that localStorage is subject to state partitioning when accessed from third-party contexts.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong>sessionStorage</strong> (): Corrected the opening paragraph which previously stated that localStorage is partitioned by origin only. Added a note about state partitioning affecting both localStorage and sessionStorage.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Web Storage API overview</strong> (): Corrected the bullet point that claimed localStorage is partitioned by origin only. Added information about state partitioning.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto">These changes address the issue that the documentation incorrectly states localStorage is partitioned by origin only, which is no longer accurate due to state partitioning mechanisms in modern browsers.</p>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43255.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3994738752" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43255" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43255/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43255">#43255</a></p>]]></content>
